      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no check that the incoming request corresponds to an active authenticated session before delegating local logout. A POST to /plugins/saml/callback with a structurally valid but maliciously crafted LogoutResponse that passes validateCredentials (e.g., a replayed response) will trigger logoutLocally even if there is no authenticated user. While logoutLocally itself safely handles a missing session via request.getSession(false), the chain is still invoked unnecessarily with the synthetic logout request, which may have side effects.",
